# Deliberate changes to content a release already shipped, which released-uuids.sh lets through
# (LE-399, IMPLEMENTATION.md section 9).
#
# One entry per line: a var key (var.concept.x.uuid), a key=uuid pair, or a bare uuid. Everything
# after " #" is the reason, and every entry must have one. An entry for a variable also covers
# the CSV rows defined through it.
#
# Adding an entry needs a SECOND REVIEWER. A database that loaded the released value keeps it, so
# the reason must say how every such database is repaired (docs/runbooks/sync-operations.md
# section 17) and who does it. Prefer not to need an entry: restore the released value, retire a
# row with Void/Retire instead of deleting it, and add new metadata under a new key.
